    python -m scripts.sweep_report out/c15_rerank/d<DEPTH>

  Read in this order and stop at the first failure.

    1. RERANK_k64_r32 against DENSE. The arm costs 1.0011x, so ANY gain beyond
       the +/-0.004 noise floor is Pareto-positive. No gain means the rank
       ceiling is not binding at d=512 and the direction closes.
    2. TEMP. If a per-token scalar captures most of the gain, the effect is one
       free parameter, not a mechanism, and not a paper.
    3. RERANK_full_r32. If it matches the top-k arm, the restriction is not doing
       the work and this is a cheap-MoS paper, which is incremental.
    4. MOS2_r32. The published comparator. The mechanism has to beat it.
    5. rank_effective_rank across the arms. DENSE should sit at its d+1 ceiling
       (c05 measured 256 of 257); the correction should visibly exceed it.
